<title>NIGERIA: Nigeria's weekly forex demand rises to $77.36 mln.</title>
<headline>Nigeria's weekly forex demand rises to $77.36 mln.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigeria's Central Bank said on Friday it sold $77.36 million at a rate of 85 to the dollar at its weekly auction this week.</p>
<p>Last week the bank sold $65.88 million at the rate of 85 naira to the dollar.</p>
<p>No reasons were given for the rise in demand. The bank last week devalued the value of the naira by 5.8 percent.</p>
<p>($1=85)</p>
<p>--Lagos newsroom +234 1 263 03 17</p>
